  "description": "The recommended STARTING set for Lyntai — not the whole library (5 of 11 packages). You get: the core library, the basic backends (the claude/codex CLIs, any OpenAI-shaped endpoint for chat, embeddings or reranking, Ollama's native API, an in-process model2vec embedder), both halves of MCP, IN-MEMORY storage, and FILE storage you switch on by naming a root (UseFileSystemStorage). Two things to know: nothing persists until you name that root (UseInMemoryStorage keeps storage in process), and for a database ADD Lyntai.Storage.Sqlite (or .Postgres); and image/video/audio generation is NOT included — add Lyntai.Generation. Also opt-in: Lyntai.Providers.LlamaSharp (in-process GGUF), Lyntai.Providers.Onnx (in-process transformers) and Lyntai.Secrets.Dpapi (Windows). Everything left out is left out because it drags a native payload, a platform-specific API, or a dependency an application that did not ask for that feature should not carry.",
